<main class="qt-wrap pt-10 md:pt-16">
    <div class="grid gap-10 lg:grid-cols-12 lg:gap-14 items-start">
        <section class="lg:col-span-7 lg:pt-4">
            <p class="qt-kicker mb-5">Calculators for Indian money</p>
            <h1 class="qt-h1 max-w-[17ch]">Loans, tax, savings and amounts in words, worked out the Indian way.</h1>
            <p class="qt-lede mt-6">Lakh and crore, the old and new tax regimes, the GST 2.0 rates, cheque wording. The sums run in your browser, and pages that depend on a rule or a rate link to the official source and say when they last changed.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="lg:col-span-5 w-full" aria-labelledby="quick-words">
            <div class="qt-sheet p-5 md:p-6">
                <label id="quick-words" for="homeAmount" class="qt-label">Amount in words</label>
                <input id="homeAmount" type="text" value="15,00,000" autocomplete="off" autocapitalize="off" spellcheck="false" maxlength="80"
                    class="qt-input qt-input-xl" placeholder="15,00,000 or 1.5 crore" oninput="homeConvert()">
                <div class="qt-slip mt-4" aria-live="polite">
                    <p class="qt-answer"><span id="homeWords" class="qt-mark">Fifteen Lakh Rupees Only</span></p>
                    <p id="homeDigits" class="qt-figure text-muted mt-2">₹15,00,000, or 1.5 million</p>
                    <p id="homeError" class="hidden mt-2 text-sm font-semibold text-stamp"></p>
                </div>
                <p class="mt-4 text-sm"><a id="homeMore" class="qt-link" href="/number-to-words/">Cheque wording and every format</a></p>
            </div>
        </section>
    </div>

    <section class="qt-index mt-16 md:mt-24" aria-label="All tools">
        {% for g in tools %}
        <div class="grid gap-3 lg:grid-cols-12 lg:gap-14 {% if not loop.first %}mt-10{% endif %}">
            <h2 class="lg:col-span-3 lg:pt-3">{{ g.group }}</h2>
            <div class="lg:col-span-9 border-t-[1.5px] border-ink">
                {% for t in g.tools %}
                {% set changed = collections.all | lastChanged(t.url) %}
                <a href="{{ t.url }}" class="qt-index-row">
                    <span class="qt-index-name">{{ t.name }}</span>
                    <span class="qt-index-desc">{{ t.desc }}</span>
                    <span class="qt-index-date">{% if changed %}Updated {{ changed | humanDate }}{% endif %}</span>
                </a>
                {% endfor %}
            </div>
        </div>
        {% endfor %}
    </section>

    <section class="grid gap-3 lg:grid-cols-12 lg:gap-14 mt-16 md:mt-24">
        <h2 class="lg:col-span-3 font-serif text-[1.35rem] font-semibold lg:pt-1">How these tools are kept right</h2>
        <div class="lg:col-span-9 qt-article">
            <p>Tax slabs, GST rates and small-savings interest rates change every year or every quarter, so a calculator is only as good as its last check. When a rule changes, the page that uses it is updated and the change is written down on the <a href="/updates/">updates page</a>, with the date.</p>
            <p>Where a page depends on a rule, it links to the body that sets it: the Income Tax Department, the GST Council, the Reserve Bank of India or the Ministry of Finance for small-savings rates. The figures here are for planning. Before you sign a loan or file a return, confirm the numbers with the lender or a tax professional.</p>
            <p>Found a figure that looks wrong? Write to <a href="mailto:quicktoolsindiaa@gmail.com">quicktoolsindiaa@gmail.com</a> and it will be checked.</p>
        </div>
    </section>
</main>

{% block scripts %}
<script src="/js/number-words.js"></script>
<script>
    function homeConvert() {
        var value = document.getElementById('homeAmount').value;
        var r = NumberWords.convert(value);
        var err = document.getElementById('homeError');
        var words = document.getElementById('homeWords');
        var digits = document.getElementById('homeDigits');
        if (r.empty || r.error) {
            err.textContent = r.error || '';
            err.classList.toggle('hidden', !r.error);
            words.parentElement.style.opacity = '.35';
            return;
        }
        err.classList.add('hidden');
        words.parentElement.style.opacity = '';
        // Digits typed: show the words. Lakh or crore typed: show the digits.
        if (r.hasUnits) {
            words.textContent = '₹' + r.indianGrouped;
            digits.textContent = r.inWords;
        } else {
            words.textContent = r.inWords;
            digits.textContent = '₹' + r.indianGrouped + ', or ' + r.internationalFormat.toLowerCase();
        }
        words.parentElement.classList.remove('qt-ink');
        void words.parentElement.offsetWidth;
        words.parentElement.classList.add('qt-ink');
        document.getElementById('homeMore').href = '/number-to-words/?n=' + encodeURIComponent(value.trim());
    }
    homeConvert();
</script>
{% endblock %}
